{"team":"KC","col":"#FF4D57","identity":"pass-heavy","funnel":"balanced-D","plays_pg":61.5,"adot":7.1,"report_html":"<div class=\"report\"><h2>Air Raid</h2><p>KC throw by design. They pass <strong>+5%</strong> over expectation (league -2%) and keep firing even with a lead (50% early-down pass when ahead vs ~41%) \u2014 the kind of pass-first identity that keeps receivers live in every script.</p><h3>The Offensive Blueprint</h3><p>There's no bell-cow to bank on \u2014 the lead back sees just <strong>50%</strong> of carries (league ~59%), a committee that caps any one back's ceiling and makes their rushing props matchup- and script-dependent.</p><p><strong>Travis Kelce</strong> is a genuine centerpiece, not an afterthought \u2014 <strong>22%</strong> of targets (league ~15%).</p><p>They spread the ball as much as anyone \u2014 the WR1 commands only <strong>16%</strong> of targets (league ~23%). Volume is democratic here, which suppresses any single receiver's ceiling but props up the TE and secondary options.</p><p>They live in the shotgun (80% of snaps vs ~68%) \u2014 a spread, pass-oriented structure.</p><p>When they fall behind they abandon the run entirely \u2014 61% pass while trailing, so their pass-catchers have huge comeback-script ceilings.</p><p><strong>Patrick Mahomes</strong> is a scramble threat \u2014 he takes off on <strong>4.8%</strong> of dropbacks (nearly double the 3.3% norm), rushing production that both lifts his own yardage and siphons a few carries from the backfield.</p><p>By the numbers it's an efficient unit \u2014 a 46% success rate (above the 44% average).</p><h3>In the Red Zone</h3><p>Inside the 20 they stay aggressive, throwing <strong>56%</strong> of the time, which puts scoring equity on <strong>Rashee Rice</strong>. And with the TE commanding 22% of targets, <strong>Travis Kelce</strong> is a live red-zone option too.</p><h2>Defense \u2014 A Balanced Defense</h2><p>They lock down opposing WR1s \u2014 just 50 rec yds/game (vs ~58); fade receiving props there.</p><p>They surrender <strong>108 rushing</strong> and <strong>220 passing</strong> yards per game (league ~120 / ~230). No dominant funnel \u2014 read it matchup by matchup.</p><h2>The Betting Angles</h2><p>Bottom line: <strong>Rashee Rice</strong> holds value even when they're winning; their pass-catchers have massive ceilings in comeback scripts (fade-material as underdogs).</p><p><em>Built on 2024\u201325 data; the profile rebuilds through the season as the current staff and roster set their own tendencies.</em></p></div>","depth":{"QB":[{"name":"Patrick Mahomes","slot":"QB1","starter":true,"td":14,"props":{"Comp":22.57,"Att":33.76,"Pass Yds":249.07,"Pass TD":1.77,"INT":0.58,"Rush Yds":21.32},"d":{"completions":22.57,"attempts":33.76,"pass_yards":249.07,"pass_td":1.77,"interceptions":0.58,"rush_att":3.73,"rush_yards":21.32}}],"RB":[{"name":"Kenneth Walker III","slot":"RB1","starter":true,"td":46,"props":{"Rush Att":23.88,"Rush Yds":105.06,"Tgt":4.82,"Rec":3.95,"Rec Yds":29.66},"d":{"rush_att":23.88,"rush_yards":105.06,"targets":4.82,"receptions":3.95,"rec_yards":29.66,"rec_td":0.07}},{"name":"Emmett Johnson","slot":"RB2","starter":true,"td":14,"props":{"Rush Att":4.11,"Rush Yds":16.92,"Tgt":1.68,"Rec":1.13,"Rec Yds":8.16},"d":{"rush_att":4.11,"rush_yards":16.92,"targets":1.68,"receptions":1.13,"rec_yards":8.16,"rec_td":0.04}},{"name":"Brashard Smith","slot":"RB3","starter":false,"td":15,"props":{"Rush Att":4.93,"Rush Yds":18.11,"Tgt":3.24,"Rec":2.08,"Rec Yds":14.39},"d":{"rush_att":4.93,"rush_yards":18.11,"targets":3.24,"receptions":2.08,"rec_yards":14.39,"rec_td":0.07}}],"WR":[{"name":"Rashee Rice","slot":"WR1","starter":true,"td":42,"props":{"Tgt":12.22,"Rec":9.11,"Rec Yds":104.27,"Rec TD":0.55},"d":{"targets":12.22,"receptions":9.11,"rec_yards":104.27,"rec_td":0.55}},{"name":"Xavier Worthy","slot":"WR2","starter":true,"td":20,"props":{"Tgt":6.49,"Rec":4.11,"Rec Yds":48.87,"Rec TD":0.23},"d":{"targets":6.49,"receptions":4.11,"rec_yards":